===== LTE modem details =====
The ZTE MF287 Pro's modem is a ZTE device powered by Qualcomm Technologies, Inc MDM9650 and running a modified Android system with Linux 3.18.31.

Installing [[:packages:pkgdata:adb|adb]] in OpenWrt enables access to a root shell of the internal modem by running ''adb shell'' from OpenWrt console. This is not necessary for normal operation.

The modem's AT command port is usually accessible in OpenWrt via ''/dev/ttyUSB1'', and can be interacted with a //terminal// app like ''picocom''.

With OpenWrt's QMI-based default configuration, the cellular modem will initiate a connection to the ISP via an Access Point Name (APN) that is defined and configured in the modem's internal configuration. To view the available list of APNs as per the modem, you may use the ''AT+CGDCONT?'' command, as illustrated below.

It is important that the APN parameters match up with your ISP's profile expectations to get a proper connection to the Internet provisioned. Your ISP should have documentation about that available somewhere in its website, or via customer service.

As a starting point, here's what was necessary to configure both in the modem and in OpenWrt to have proper dual-stack Internet working with a [[https://www.yesss.at/|yesss! (Austria, EU) LTE pre-paid contract]] in 2024:

